                                            "value": "Compose AR-field and AR-geometry with analytic boundary trajectories. Use simulation-health capability, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/simulation-health-diagnostics.md for approved horizons and temporary probes; project oracles must be implemented. Test local displaced volume, wall flux and pressure work directly. Where the approved references require tagged transport, use a bounded fixture-only tracer/reference probe over the actual geometric and flow fluxes, not a second production transport path. It must neither require T-species nor claim full species-solver acceptance. Retain negative or inconclusive outcomes as valid experiment results."
                                        },
                                        {
                                            "field": "acceptance_criteria",
                                            "value": [
                                                "Uniform-pressure equilibrium, free expansion, sealed moving barriers, moving corners, and support changes are tested across approved refinements.",
                                                "Local displaced volume, wall flux and wall work are checked independently of global balances; any bounded tracer/reference probe records its scope and limitations and is not full species-transport qualification.",
                                                "Timestep, pressure convergence, small-cell work, memory, and complete prescribed-boundary cost are reported against approved limits.",
                                                "The report identifies failed, passed, and inconclusive conditions and does not equate experiment completion with adoption."
                                            ]
                                        }
                                    ],
                                    "op": "update_fields",
                                    "target": {
                                        "id": "T-moving-field",
