        "response": "{\n  \"status\": \"ready\",\n  \"vision_summary\": \"Establish an independently runnable Substrate foundation through an approved, bounded coupled-organism experiment: deformable tissue, honest pressure-bearing contents, moving-boundary environmental flow, nutrient transport, and fuel-limited actuation. Qualify physical behavior, accumulated error, and complete cost before a separate interacting-population rejection screen. The rich world, evolution, and broader material features remain later scope.\",\n  \"assumptions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A-scope\",\n      \"statement\": \"This initial plan delivers the first coupled proof and a subsequent 16-organism screening fixture, not the complete 256-organism rich world. Damage, repair, reproduction, thermal state, general fracture, automatic representation switching, and evolutionary control are deferred.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A-candidate\",\n      \"statement\": \"The provisional candidate is connected deformable structures, well-mixed inertial chambers, and a conservative Cartesian cut-cell fluid/transport field. Its numerical details and suitability require design, human approval, and measured adoption evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A-habitat\",\n      \"statement\": \"The initial habitat is completely liquid-filled with declared pressure/open boundaries that can accommodate changing organism area. A sealed incompressible box with independently expanding contents is not assumed physically compatible.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A-hardware\",\n      \"statement\": \"The Ryzen 9 9950X3D with up to 16 CPU workers is the proposed performance reference. If unavailable, results are diagnostic rather than reference-hardware acceptance unless the user explicitly approves a substitute.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A-screen\",\n      \"statement\": \"The proposed 16-organism laboratory target is used only after its geometry, supported interactions, numerical quality, and measurement protocol are approved. A short population screen can reject the candidate but cannot establish rich-world endurance.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"architecture\": {\n    \"summary\": \"One project-owned simulation core maintains authoritative committed state and a bounded transactional advancement schedule. Compact structural mechanics, chamber contents, and fluid control volumes have disjoint ownership of mass and species. A shared geometry/exchange layer makes occupied area, boundary flux, pressure work, and collision barriers agree. Local controllers submit resource-limited requests rather than modifying physical state. A thin Bitloop shell provides construction, presentation, replay, and project-owned diagnostic adapters. Numerical adoption is conditional, not implied by construction.\",\n    \"components\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-state\",\n        \"name\": \"Authoritative state and advancement\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Own stable structural/material references, committed time, inventory ownership, staging, bounded retries, validity checks, and atomic interval acceptance.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-structure\",\n        \"name\": \"Deformable structures\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Represent tissue, membrane edges, area-bearing elements, and contractile attachments; integrate mass, constitutive forces, reactions, and supported contact.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-contents\",\n        \"name\": \"Chamber contents\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Own well-mixed enclosed inventories, mass/inertia approximation, geometry-derived pressure and stored energy, and finite exchange ports.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-field\",\n        \"name\": \"Fluid and transported fields\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Own environmental liquid, momentum, and species amounts; solve conservative flow and transport with declared outer conditions.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-interface\",\n        \"name\": \"Geometry and conservative coupling\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Derive cut geometry, side-separated membrane barriers, swept volumes, pressure traction, paired impulse/work exchanges, and opening/permeability connectivity.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-biology\",\n        \"name\": \"Local resource processes\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Apply finite transfers, reactions, local sensing, deterministic control, and fuel-limited actuator requests without privileged state edits.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-app\",\n        \"name\": \"Construction and Bitloop shell\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Construct experimental organisms, own engine instances, request fixed simulated intervals, and expose camera, drawing, configuration, replay, and explicit restart adapters.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"C-evidence\",\n        \"name\": \"Project diagnostics and fixtures\",\n        \"responsibility\": \"Provide physical oracles, semantic telemetry, bounded health checks, full-cost benchmarks, inspected snapshots, and reproducible experiment configurations outside the core.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relationships\": [\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-state\",\n        \"to\": \"C-structure\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Schedules staged mechanical updates and commits only valid coupled state.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-state\",\n        \"to\": \"C-contents\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Owns transaction boundaries for chamber state and inventory changes.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-state\",\n        \"to\": \"C-field\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Coordinates fluid updates, conserved reductions, solver failures, and commit.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-structure\",\n        \"to\": \"C-interface\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Supplies oriented boundary topology, positions, velocities, and material-side identity.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-interface\",\n        \"to\": \"C-field\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Supplies fluid-accessible geometry, side connectivity, swept volume, and wall flux constraints; receives pressure and fluid reactions.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-interface\",\n        \"to\": \"C-structure\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Returns paired boundary impulses and measured work using the same geometry as displacement.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-contents\",\n        \"to\": \"C-interface\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Uses actual chamber area and its variation for pressure, wall work, and finite physical ports.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-biology\",\n        \"to\": \"C-state\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Submits local sensing-derived transfers and actuator requests through validated staged interfaces.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-app\",\n        \"to\": \"C-state\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Constructs supported state and requests complete simulated intervals independent of rendering.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-evidence\",\n        \"to\": \"C-state\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Reads committed-state observations and invokes fixtures without making diagnostics a core dependency.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"from\": \"C-app\",\n        \"to\": \"C-evidence\",\n        \"relationship\": \"Routes Bitloop headless traces, captures, replay, and checkpoint operations through project-owned adapters.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"decisions\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"D-scope\",\n        \"decision\": \"Adopt an evidence-gated foundation project, not an implementation of the entire long-term vision.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"A small coupled proof must expose unsuitable representations before population complexity or broad biology makes them expensive to replace.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"D-core\",\n        \"decision\": \"Keep simulation state, constitutive laws, topology, and advancement independent of Scene, UI, rendering, scenario names, trace formats, and file output.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"This preserves ownership, focused testing, and an independently buildable core while reusing Bitloop facilities.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"D-method\",\n        \"decision\": \"Investigate one CPU candidate: compact connected structures, inertial well-mixed chambers, and conservative cut-cell grid flow with side-separated barriers.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"It directly tests the preferred inexpensive representation without a universal particle solver, backend menu, GPU dependency, or speculative extension framework.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"D-contract\",\n        \"decision\": \"Freeze units, supported geometry, discrete exchange laws, error budgets, solver/retry limits, horizons, and cost accounting before the adoption campaign.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Passing global accounts or relaxing tolerances after failure cannot establish correct local behavior.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"D-transaction\",\n        \"decision\": \"Use one authoritative committed state with staged updates and bounded failure handling; never skip requested simulated time.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"All coupled owners must roll back together, including resources and controller phase, without requiring an unmeasured deep copy at every substep.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"D-energy\",\n        \"decision\": \"Keep physical work, stored energy, physical dissipation, metabolic conversion, and numerical residual separate.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Numerical loss must not become heat or fuel, and global corrections must not conceal passive propulsion or local transport errors.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"D-ownership\",\n        \"decision\": \"Use only project-owned implementation and public Bitloop facilities; framework or broader dependency changes require explicit user authorization immediately before writing.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Capability declarations neither establish implemented hooks nor authorize changes outside Substrate.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"D-gates\",\n        \"decision\": \"Require a human-approved first work package, reviewed representative coupled adoption evidence, and a separate population screen.\",\n        \"rationale\": \"Design approval, experiment completion, numerical adoption, and scale claims are different decisions.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-bootstrap\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Run a supervised Bitloop and MindGraph pilot\",\n      \"goal\": \"Establish the smallest real project-owned build, headless observation, and saved-result handoff without implementing physics.\",\n      \"context\": \"Use capability bitloop, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/bitloop.md and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md; use traces, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md and references/tracing-diagnostics.md under that skill. Identify the active target and exact APIs. Preserve user build state and ownership boundaries D-core/D-ownership. This bounded pilot may add minimal project-owned telemetry, not a diagnostics framework. Record tested claims, source/build identity, actual commands, failed or unverified checks, and substantive observations in supported MindGraph result fields.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-app\", \"C-evidence\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"The smallest relevant target is built in a Codex-owned context and a real Bitloop headless run identifies the selected scene and fixed-step observations.\",\n        \"The result distinguishes existing hooks from implemented adapters and retains compact evidence under .codex/runs.\",\n        \"Instruction conflicts, unavailable tooling, and external-owner changes are reported rather than bypassed.\",\n        \"The worker publishes its result without attempting to verify its own subsequent persisted completion or review.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Does the pilot expose missing project hooks, ownership conflicts, or evidence-routing failures that prevent the planned supervised workflow?\"\n      },\n      \"input_artifacts\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-loop-confirm\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Confirm the completed management loop\",\n      \"goal\": \"Verify execution, saved result, review, and reload before substantial numerical work.\",\n      \"context\": \"A supervisor or workflow owner examines the completed T-bootstrap result after its review. This is not simulator implementation. Check that substantive observations survive persistence and reload; keep management repairs in their owning project.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-evidence\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-bootstrap\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"The persisted and reloaded pilot result contains its actual observations, limitations, and evidence references, and the triggered review is visible.\",\n        \"Missing context, misleading acceptance, instruction conflicts, or evidence loss have minimal reproducers.\",\n        \"Numerical work remains blocked while a consequential workflow failure is unresolved.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Establish and approve the bounded numerical work package\",\n      \"goal\": \"Resolve the candidate's substantive mechanisms and acceptance policy before implementation.\",\n      \"context\": \"Children establish separate physical and numerical contracts, reconcile them, and obtain explicit human approval. A-scope and D-method bound the work.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-state\", \"C-structure\", \"C-contents\", \"C-field\", \"C-interface\", \"C-biology\", \"C-evidence\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-loop-confirm\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"The reconciled package contains worked references for all implemented mechanisms and compatible global boundary conditions.\",\n        \"Implementation is released only through the separate human decision task.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-budgets\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Define experiments, validity ranges, and budgets\",\n      \"goal\": \"Turn proposed physical and performance requirements into a bounded, reviewable experimental specification.\",\n      \"context\": \"Use A-scope/A-hardware/A-screen and D-contract. Define the smallest two-chamber contractile organism that swims and pumps through finite ports, with nutrient exchange and fuel use; it need not represent a named substance. Specify consistent 2D units, shapes, coefficients, minimum features, fixed resolution family, initial conditions, species and energy meanings, and environmental outer conditions. Define prototype and later 16-organism screen separately; do not adopt the 256-organism workload. Numerical tolerances are proposals for human approval, not facts supplied by the vision.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-evidence\", \"C-app\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-loop-confirm\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Reference cases cover translation, rotation, pressure equilibrium, free expansion, compression/recovery, advection, diffusion, sealed moving barriers, pumping, and fuel exhaustion.\",\n        \"Local and cumulative error budgets use relevant motion and resource scales, include passive propulsion and weak-motion loss, and specify refinement comparisons.\",\n        \"Campaigns have predeclared time/compute limits, timescale-derived horizons, extension rules, rejection/inconclusive outcomes, and supported event coverage.\",\n        \"The 16-organism proposal preserves up to 128 vertices, two chambers, 16 actuators per organism, 128 by 128 active cells, and the proposed real-time target; exclusions and actual active counts are explicit.\",\n        \"Complete cost includes staging, solves, safety scans, retries, and commit; memory categories, hardware reporting, rendering, recording, and checkpoint accounting are specified.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-state-design\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Define authoritative state and shared data ownership\",\n      \"goal\": \"Establish minimal core types and ownership boundaries before mechanisms depend on them.\",\n      \"context\": \"Consume the experiment specification. Define stable handles for structures, chambers, regions and inventories; dense storage is private. Specify positions, velocities, mass, chamber inventories, field amounts, boundary-side identifiers, port endpoints, controller phase, committed time, and observable accounts. Exclude serialization format and universal registries.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-state\", \"C-interface\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-budgets\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Every mass, species amount, momentum contribution, and stored energy has one authoritative owner.\",\n        \"Minimal read views and staged request/result shapes include units, signs, validity conditions, and unsupported-state errors.\",\n        \"A worked ownership example follows a nutrient amount from field through a chamber and reaction without duplicate ownership.\",\n        \"Derived caches and immutable configuration are distinguished from rollback-relevant state.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-experiments\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-mechanics-design\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Specify passive structural mechanics\",\n      \"goal\": \"Choose the bounded tissue and membrane discretization with measurable deformation and work error.\",\n      \"context\": \"Use D-method and the shared state contract. Specify mass allocation, compliant edge/area/shear response, damping, integration, element inversion/degeneracy handling, timestep restrictions, and attachment forces. No population contact, damage, general remeshing, or rigid-region implementation is required here.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-structure\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-budgets\", \"T-state-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Discrete forces or constraints, solver stopping rules, and physical versus numerical dissipation are explicit.\",\n        \"Worked stretch, shear, compression/recovery, rigid translation, and rotation cases establish mass, force, torque, energy, and deformation oracles.\",\n        \"Feature collapse and inversion produce bounded rejection rather than silent deletion or stiffness changes.\",\n        \"Actuator attachment and boundary impulse interfaces are defined without implementing active laws.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-experiments\", \"AR-state-contract\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-contents-design\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Specify chamber inertia, pressure, and wall work\",\n      \"goal\": \"Give cheap contents an honest mechanical meaning separate from tissue mass.\",\n      \"context\": \"Define the well-mixed chamber approximation using actual oriented chamber geometry. Choose a bounded inertia model with stated limitations; do not treat contents as massless pressure or double-count them as environmental fluid. Establish compatibility between the chamber pressure law and A-habitat.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-contents\", \"C-interface\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-budgets\", \"T-state-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Pressure, stored energy, mass/inertia, concentration, and geometric area use one consistent discrete meaning.\",\n        \"Worked translation, rotation, free expansion, and compression examples show wall reactions and work signs.\",\n        \"Finite inflow/outflow specifies transferred mass, momentum, and energy without invented ejection speed.\",\n        \"Unsupported sloshing, stratification, shape degeneracy, and low-inventory states have explicit detection and failure policies.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-experiments\", \"AR-state-contract\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-field-design\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Specify the stationary fluid and transport equations\",\n      \"goal\": \"Define the conservative field solver and species transport before introducing moving geometry.\",\n      \"context\": \"Choose the discrete incompressible liquid momentum/pressure formulation, viscosity treatment, face fluxes, and conservative advection/diffusion for the declared species. Specify compatible open/pressure outer conditions, pressure null-space treatment where applicable, and initial/boundary data. Keep geometry operators abstract only at the explicit interface consumed by T-geometry-design.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-field\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-budgets\", \"T-state-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Discrete equations, stored quantities, pressure convergence measures, positivity conditions, and bounded solver work are specified.\",\n        \"Worked stationary pressure, channel flow, uniform advection, and diffusion references establish local as well as global oracles.\",\n        \"Boundary inflow/outflow accounts close material, momentum, species, and work consistently.\",\n        \"The specification defines required geometry inputs and flux outputs, including disconnected fluid regions.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-experiments\", \"AR-state-contract\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-geometry-design\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Specify moving cut geometry and compatible exchanges\",\n      \"goal\": \"Resolve geometric conservation, thin barriers, pressure traction, and small-cell treatment.\",\n      \"context\": \"Consume the field equations and boundary state definitions. Specify fluid-accessible subregions, oriented faces, membrane-side connectivity, swept areas, newly uncovered material treatment, and the relationship between divergence and pressure force. Choose one bounded small-cell stabilization strategy that does not merge opposite sides of a membrane.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-interface\", \"C-field\", \"C-structure\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-budgets\", \"T-state-design\", \"T-field-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Worked translating/rotating wall, expanding chamber, moving corner, and supported narrow-passage examples establish swept-volume and local transport identities.\",\n        \"Thin barriers prevent interpolation or ordinary cell mixing between opposite sides.\",\n        \"A support-change example shows continuous physical response, including pressure work and remapping error.\",\n        \"Small-cell thresholds, stabilization limits, memory growth, timestep consequences, and unsupported geometry errors are explicit.\",\n        \"The same boundary definition supports later mechanical contact and impermeable field barriers.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-experiments\", \"AR-state-contract\", \"AR-field-design\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-transfer-design\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Specify finite ports, permeability, and reactions\",\n      \"goal\": \"Define resource movement and conversion independently of actuation.\",\n      \"context\": \"Use declared species, chamber state, and field face/port interfaces. Specify finite channel conductance, permeable flux, local sampling, reaction stoichiometry and rates, donor availability, simultaneous competing requests, and paired recipient updates. No rupture, growth, repair, or thermal conversion is implemented in this scope.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-biology\", \"C-contents\", \"C-field\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-budgets\", \"T-state-design\", \"T-contents-design\", \"T-field-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Worked two-chamber flow and chamber-to-field permeability examples have finite rates, paired inventories, and correct transferred momentum/work where applicable.\",\n        \"Competing drains cannot overspend a donor; exhausted donors and rejected transactions leave no negative or duplicate amounts.\",\n        \"Reaction examples close declared constituent and energy accounts, with explicit waste and sources/sinks.\",\n        \"Connections do not imply instantaneous mixing, and spatial sampling never crosses an intact barrier.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-experiments\", \"AR-state-contract\", \"AR-contents-design\", \"AR-field-design\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-actuation-design\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Specify local control and work-limited contraction\",\n      \"goal\": \"Define how local sensing and finite fuel constrain mechanical activity.\",\n      \"context\": \"Define deterministic controller inputs, update cadence, actuator requests, accepted work, and reaction outputs. Use scripted cycles for physical references and a local deterministic controller for the demonstration. Controllers must not set positions, choose solver settings, or read unrestricted world state.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-biology\", \"C-structure\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-budgets\", \"T-state-design\", \"T-mechanics-design\", \"T-transfer-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"A worked contraction cycle defines force/displacement work signs, available fuel, efficiency, and nonpositive-work policy without generating fuel from numerical residuals.\",\n        \"Fuel exhaustion bounds delivered work and request changes cannot inject unaccounted mechanical energy.\",\n        \"Controller cadence integrates elapsed simulated time and rolls back phase and resource requests on failure.\",\n        \"Local sensing footprint, latency, and gradient validity limits are explicit.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-experiments\", \"AR-state-contract\", \"AR-mechanics-design\", \"AR-transfer-design\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-schedule-design\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Reconcile coupling, advancement, and failure semantics\",\n      \"goal\": \"Assemble the separate mechanisms into one implementable work package without concealing missing laws.\",\n      \"context\": \"Reconcile all named design outputs. Specify the coupled substep order, time centering, geometry/pressure/mechanics iteration, conservation reductions, resource reservation and commit order, solver and retry ceilings, and staging cost model. Identify unresolved contradictions rather than silently choosing replacement mechanisms.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-state\", \"C-interface\", \"C-structure\", \"C-contents\", \"C-field\", \"C-biology\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-budgets\", \"T-state-design\", \"T-mechanics-design\", \"T-contents-design\", \"T-field-design\", \"T-geometry-design\", \"T-transfer-design\", \"T-actuation-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"A complete worked substep follows geometry, impulses, pressure work, field fluxes, reactions, fuel, and commit using the mechanism specifications.\",\n        \"A deliberately rejected substep leaves every authoritative owner and actual simulated time unchanged; bounded retry exhaustion returns an actionable failure.\",\n        \"Changing occupied area is compatible with outer flow conditions and chamber compressibility.\",\n        \"The package publishes proposed tolerances, supported resolutions, bounded campaign budgets, and explicit stop conditions without claiming approval.\",\n        \"Unresolved design obligations and expected whole-step cost risks are listed for review.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Do the reconciled mechanisms in D-method form a physically compatible and affordable candidate, or do chamber inertia, moving cut geometry, pressure work, or bounded coupling require redesign before approval?\"\n      },\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-experiments\", \"AR-state-contract\", \"AR-mechanics-design\", \"AR-contents-design\", \"AR-field-design\", \"AR-geometry-design\", \"AR-transfer-design\", \"AR-actuation-design\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-approve\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Obtain human approval of the first physical work package\",\n      \"goal\": \"Release implementation only after explicit approval of scope, approximation, budgets, and experiments.\",\n      \"context\": \"Present AR-work-package after the T-schedule-design review. Approval is a workflow decision, not an artifact inferred from the package's existence. Any requested physical or budget change must update the affected design before release.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-evidence\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-schedule-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"The human explicitly approves or rejects the candidate, validity range, error budgets, performance protocol, compute limits, and bounded scope.\",\n        \"Rejected or unresolved decisions block dependent implementation.\",\n        \"No tolerance is weakened implicitly in response to a future failing campaign.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-work-package\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Build the independently testable coupled foundation\",\n      \"goal\": \"Implement the approved candidate as focused packages before active-organism adoption.\",\n      \"context\": \"Children implement D-core/D-transaction within the approved work package. No later population, damage, repair, checkpoint, or presentation work is necessary to reach the first coupled result.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-state\", \"C-structure\", \"C-contents\", \"C-field\", \"C-interface\", \"C-biology\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-approve\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Independent mechanism tests and a reproducible active coupled fixture exist.\",\n        \"No mechanism silently departs from the approved physical contract.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-core\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement authoritative state and bounded transactions\",\n      \"goal\": \"Provide the core state, staging, time, and exchange interfaces consumed by all mechanisms.\",\n      \"context\": \"Implement the state and advancement portions of AR-work-package, including stable handles, compact storage, immutable configuration, scratch reuse, interval result/error types, and conserved accounts. Use bitloop capability via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/bitloop.md and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md for public math and CMake integration only; keep the core independent of framework lifecycle and diagnostics.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-state\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-approve\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"A focused target exercises commit, rejection, retry exhaustion, stale references, nonfinite values, and requested-versus-actual simulated time.\",\n        \"Injected failure preserves all staged-owner state and committed time.\",\n        \"Empty and representative-size staging cost and memory are measured rather than assumed negligible.\",\n        \"The implemented core API is available to downstream mechanism packages.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-work-package\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-passive\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement passive tissue and membrane mechanics\",\n      \"goal\": \"Deliver passive mechanical response independently of chambers or fluid.\",\n      \"context\": \"Implement the approved structural law and attachment interfaces using AR-core. Keep active actuation and population contact out of this task.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-structure\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-core\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Stretch, shear, compression/recovery, translation, and rotation meet approved force, torque, deformation, and energy-error criteria.\",\n        \"Resolution/timestep comparisons expose damping and integration error.\",\n        \"Degenerate or inverted features reject safely without deleting material.\",\n        \"Focused tests retain physical versus numerical work observations.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-core\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-chambers\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement inertial pressure chambers\",\n      \"goal\": \"Add geometry-based chamber contents and wall reactions on passive structures.\",\n      \"context\": \"Implement the approved contents model using AR-passive and AR-core. Keep ports closed for these references; fluid-field coupling and reaction laws remain separate.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-contents\", \"C-structure\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-core\", \"T-passive\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Translation and rotation include contents mass/inertia exactly as specified, without duplication.\",\n        \"Pressure equilibrium, free expansion, and compression/recovery meet local geometry, pressure, and wall-work budgets.\",\n        \"Low-inventory and invalid-geometry cases follow the approved failure policy.\",\n        \"A closed chamber trajectory demonstrates bounded cumulative error over the specified passive horizon.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-core\", \"AR-passive\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-field\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement stationary fluid and conservative species transport\",\n      \"goal\": \"Establish field correctness and pressure cost before moving boundaries.\",\n      \"context\": \"Implement the approved stationary field equations on AR-core with prescribed static geometry, pressure/open boundaries, and positivity-preserving transport. This includes the declared species but not chamber transfers or reactions.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-field\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-core\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Stationary pressure, channel flow, advection, and diffusion meet the approved local-field and global-balance references.\",\n        \"Species positivity and explicit boundary source/sink accounts hold.\",\n        \"Pressure convergence, iteration ceilings, memory, and complete field-step cost are recorded at prescribed resolutions.\",\n        \"Unconverged pressure and inadmissible transport reject the staged update.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-core\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-geometry\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement shared moving-geometry operators\",\n      \"goal\": \"Provide independently testable conservative geometry and barrier connectivity.\",\n      \"context\": \"Implement the geometry portion of AR-work-package using AR-core. Do not bury geometry validation inside a fluid trajectory. Tests may prescribe boundary paths analytically.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-interface\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-core\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Analytic swept-area tests for translation, rotation, expansion, and moving corners meet local and global tolerances.\",\n        \"Membrane sides remain disconnected, including same-cell intersections and supported narrow passages.\",\n        \"Support changes and small-cell stabilization preserve approved conservation identities without merging incompatible regions.\",\n        \"Unsupported geometric features fail explicitly and operator memory/work are measured.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-core\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-moving-field\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"title\": \"Qualify prescribed-boundary fluid response\",\n      \"goal\": \"Test moving-wall displacement and pressure work without two-way mechanical feedback.\",\n      \"context\": \"Compose AR-field and AR-geometry with analytic boundary trajectories. Use simulation-health capability, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/simulation-health-diagnostics.md for approved horizons and temporary probes; project oracles must be implemented. Retain negative or inconclusive outcomes as valid experiment results.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-field\", \"C-interface\", \"C-evidence\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-field\", \"T-geometry\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Uniform-pressure equilibrium, free expansion, sealed moving barriers, moving corners, and support changes are tested across approved refinements.\",\n        \"Local volume/species transport and wall work are checked independently of global balances.\",\n        \"Timestep, pressure convergence, small-cell work, memory, and complete prescribed-boundary cost are reported against approved limits.\",\n        \"The report identifies failed, passed, and inconclusive conditions and does not equate experiment completion with adoption.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Does prescribed-boundary evidence support D-method's cut-cell/barrier treatment at the approved quality and cost, or must geometry/pressure coupling change before two-way reliance?\"\n      },\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-field\", \"AR-geometry\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-passive-coupling\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement two-way passive chamber–fluid coupling\",\n      \"goal\": \"Join passive structures, inertial contents, and environmental fluid with transactional reactions.\",\n      \"context\": \"Proceed only after favorable review of AR-moving-field. Implement the approved coupling schedule and paired impulse/work interfaces; no active biology yet. Use simulation-health via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md and references/simulation-health-diagnostics.md under .agents/skills/bitloop-development.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-state\", \"C-structure\", \"C-contents\", \"C-field\", \"C-interface\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-core\", \"T-passive\", \"T-chambers\", \"T-moving-field\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Passive equilibrium, translation/rotation, compression/recovery, and expansion satisfy local fields, momentum reactions, and approved work budgets.\",\n        \"Closed unforced cycles show no sustained unexplained energy growth or passive propulsion.\",\n        \"Injected coupling failure rolls back mechanics, contents, geometry-dependent state, fluid, and time together.\",\n        \"Complete coupled step cost includes staging, geometry, pressure iterations, safety checks, and rejected attempts.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-core\", \"AR-passive\", \"AR-chambers\", \"AR-moving-field\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-transfers\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement finite exchange and local reactions\",\n      \"goal\": \"Deliver conservative ports, permeability, and resource conversion independently of active mechanics.\",\n      \"context\": \"Implement the transfer/reaction portion of AR-work-package against field, chamber, and geometry interfaces. Exercise static or prescribed geometry first. Exclude rupture, growth, repair, and heat.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-biology\", \"C-contents\", \"C-field\", \"C-interface\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-core\", \"T-chambers\", \"T-field\", \"T-geometry\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Two-chamber transport has measured finite equilibration rather than instant mixing.\",\n        \"Permeability and real openings exchange paired species, mass, momentum, and work as specified, while sealed boundaries have forbidden flux below budget.\",\n        \"Competing donor requests, exhaustion, and rejected transactions preserve positivity and ownership.\",\n        \"Reaction tests close declared constituent and energy accounts and retain explicit waste/source/sink observations.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-core\", \"AR-chambers\", \"AR-field\", \"AR-geometry\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-actuators\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement local sensing and fuel-limited actuation\",\n      \"goal\": \"Connect bounded controller requests to paid mechanical work.\",\n      \"context\": \"Implement the approved local controller and actuator law using AR-transfers and AR-passive. Test scripted cycles and deterministic local feedback; no organism-specific swimming physics or general brain framework.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-biology\", \"C-structure\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-core\", \"T-passive\", \"T-transfers\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"A loaded actuator cycle demonstrates the approved relationship between fuel expenditure and accepted work.\",\n        \"Fuel exhaustion limits contraction, negative-work handling matches policy, and numerical residual cannot fund activity.\",\n        \"Controller reads remain local and requests cannot teleport inventory or edit physical state.\",\n        \"Replay and forced-rejection tests preserve controller cadence, resource reservations, and deterministic behavior.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-core\", \"AR-passive\", \"AR-transfers\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-prototype\",\n      \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n      \"title\": \"Construct the first active coupled organism\",\n      \"goal\": \"Deliver the smallest runnable organism demonstrating motion, pumping, nutrient exchange, and fuel limitation.\",\n      \"context\": \"Compose AR-passive-coupling, AR-transfers, and AR-actuators using the approved fixture. Use bitloop and traces capabilities via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/bitloop.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md, .agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md and its references/tracing-diagnostics.md. Keep Substrate/Substrate.h and .cpp thin; place construction and telemetry outside core ownership.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-app\", \"C-evidence\", \"C-biology\", \"C-state\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-passive-coupling\", \"T-transfers\", \"T-actuators\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"A documented headless command runs the seeded approved fixture for fixed simulated intervals independent of rendering.\",\n        \"Semantic traces expose inventories, local fluxes, chamber pressure/area, actuator fuel/work, motion, pressure iterations, retries, and actual committed time.\",\n        \"Focused integration cases show pumping against load, nutrient uptake, useful motion, and loss of actuation when fuel is exhausted.\",\n        \"A smoke run is explicitly labeled integration evidence, not adoption or endurance.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-passive-coupling\", \"AR-transfers\", \"AR-actuators\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-adoption\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Run the representative coupled adoption campaign\",\n      \"goal\": \"Determine whether the candidate preserves meaningful behavior and complete cost over approved horizons and refinements.\",\n      \"context\": \"Use AR-prototype and the frozen AR-work-package without weakening limits. Use traces and simulation-health via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md, and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/tracing-diagnostics.md and simulation-health-diagnostics.md. Run bounded refinement and repeated-cycle comparisons before population expansion. Numerical conclusions must be retained in supported result fields as well as the report.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-evidence\", \"C-state\", \"C-interface\", \"C-biology\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-prototype\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"The report compares approved resolutions/timesteps at equal simulated duration, including local transport, pressure, shape, motion, pumping work, gradients, and resource affordability.\",\n        \"Hard monitors run throughout; selected full committed-state inspections and anomaly-local probes cover relaxation, transport, forcing, and accumulation timescales.\",\n        \"Complete cost and memory include all substeps, rejected attempts, staging, coupling solves, and safety work, with actual hardware/build/precision/worker details.\",\n        \"Passive propulsion, cyclic gain, lost weak motion, feature collapse, and unresolved drift are explicitly assessed against predeclared budgets.\",\n        \"Failed or inconclusive results are retained with counterexamples; reaching the experiment's budget is not recorded as physical adoption.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Does AR-adoption justify adopting the representative coupled candidate under D-contract/D-energy, or do behavior, accumulated local error, or full cost require rejection before contact and population expansion?\"\n      },\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-prototype\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-contact-design\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Define supported population contact\",\n      \"goal\": \"Establish a bounded contact model only after the coupled foundation merits expansion.\",\n      \"context\": \"Proceed only after favorable T-adoption review. Specify broad phase, deformable membrane/terrain contact, self-contact policy, friction, impulses/work, collision time handling, narrow-gap validity, and compatibility with fluid barriers. Scope is the approved laboratory screen, not general fracture or arbitrary dense packing.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-structure\", \"C-interface\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-adoption\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Worked two-body and body–terrain contacts establish momentum, reaction, friction work, and penetration tolerances.\",\n        \"Fluid-gap closure and under-resolved passages have explicit supported limits and failure semantics, with no erased walls or mixed chamber contents.\",\n        \"Contact candidate counts, iteration/retry limits, and event-burst cost budgets are defined before implementation.\",\n        \"Any contact law that materially changes the approved physical approximation is returned for human decision rather than silently adopted.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-adoption\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-contact\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement bounded shared-world contact\",\n      \"goal\": \"Enable organisms to interact mechanically with each other and terrain in the supported habitat.\",\n      \"context\": \"Implement AR-contact-design on AR-prototype, reusing shared boundary geometry. Contact must participate in the same transaction and full-cost accounts; do not introduce a separate physics world.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-structure\", \"C-interface\", \"C-state\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-contact-design\", \"T-prototype\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Two-body, terrain, friction, self-contact-policy, and narrow-gap tests satisfy the contact contract.\",\n        \"Contact and field barriers agree during moving collisions with no forbidden inventory passage.\",\n        \"Forced collision failure rolls back the complete state and time.\",\n        \"A small interacting fixture records contact work, candidate counts, retries, and event-burst cost.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-contact-design\", \"AR-prototype\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-population-screen\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Run the separate 16-organism scale screen\",\n      \"goal\": \"Expose whole-world cost and interaction failures without claiming rich-world acceptance.\",\n      \"context\": \"Proceed only on favorable T-adoption review and within the frozen laboratory protocol. Use AR-contact and AR-work-package. Use traces and simulation-health via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md and the corresponding tracing-diagnostics.md and simulation-health-diagnostics.md references under .agents/skills/bitloop-development. All organisms sense, metabolize, and actuate; shared flow, contact, pumping, feeding, and resource competition must be active.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-app\", \"C-evidence\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-adoption\", \"T-contact\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"The reproducible fixture reports actual vertices, bonds/elements, chambers, actuators, active cells, species, controller work, and event rates rather than organism count alone.\",\n        \"Whole calculated intervals include every substep and retry; throughput, latency distribution, maximum latency, pressure work, and memory are reported on the declared machine.\",\n        \"The proposed one simulated second per wall-clock second target is evaluated at the approved quality without sleeping away biological activity.\",\n        \"Repeated windows include interactions and event bursts; negative or inconclusive evidence stops scale expansion.\",\n        \"The report explicitly states that this screen does not prove the 256-organism target or ten-minute/100-cycle rich-world endurance.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": {\n        \"question\": \"Does the interacting 16-organism screen support affordable scaling of the adopted foundation, or do shared pressure, contact, safety/staging, and transport costs invalidate A-screen and require a new representation decision?\"\n      },\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-adoption\", \"AR-contact\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-presentation\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Deliver an inspectable prototype laboratory\",\n      \"goal\": \"Expose the accepted prototype through a thin visual shell without making rendering part of the physics.\",\n      \"context\": \"Proceed after favorable T-adoption review; this work need not wait for the population screen. Use bitloop and snapshots-checkpoints capabilities via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/bitloop.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/snapshots-checkpoints.md, .agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md and references/checkpoints-snapshots.md and visual-qa.md. Capture support must be checked; this task does not implement checkpoint serialization.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-app\", \"C-evidence\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-adoption\", \"T-prototype\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"A human can launch, pause, single-step, and inspect the representative organism with declared units and actual simulated time.\",\n        \"Drawing shows structure, chamber boundaries, relevant flow/species fields, and fuel/work observations without changing authoritative state.\",\n        \"Inspected snapshots correlate with semantic state and show distinguishable healthy, depleted, and stopped-error states.\",\n        \"Rendering cost is measured separately and the run remains independent of render cadence.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-adoption\", \"AR-prototype\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-restart\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Implement explicit restart and reproducible recordings\",\n      \"goal\": \"Make accepted prototype experiments restartable and recordable on a declared execution configuration.\",\n      \"context\": \"Proceed after favorable T-adoption review. Use snapshots-checkpoints and traces via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/snapshots-checkpoints.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/checkpoints-snapshots.md and tracing-diagnostics.md. Generated checkpoint hooks are not assumed implemented. Serialize authoritative state, controller/RNG state, configuration identity and actual time; rebuild derived caches. No cross-hardware bitwise promise.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-app\", \"C-state\", \"C-evidence\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-adoption\", \"T-core\", \"T-prototype\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"Explicit save/load rejects incompatible or malformed checkpoints without modifying valid running state.\",\n        \"Uninterrupted and save/restore continuations agree by declared fingerprints or approved tolerances, including resource/work accounts and controller phase.\",\n        \"Seeded replay repeats accepted behavior on the declared configuration.\",\n        \"A recording command reports physics, rendering, capture/checkpoint I/O, and total user-facing throughput separately.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-adoption\", \"AR-core\", \"AR-prototype\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"T-handoff\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Publish the bounded foundation and its limits\",\n      \"goal\": \"Deliver runnable examples, qualification conclusions, and an honest statement of what remains unproven.\",\n      \"context\": \"Integrate presentation, restart, and population-screen findings without new physical mechanisms. If a review rejects the foundation, publish the negative findings and do not label it adopted. Reuse the existing project documentation rather than creating a competing roadmap.\",\n      \"components\": [\"C-app\", \"C-evidence\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [\"T-presentation\", \"T-restart\", \"T-population-screen\", \"T-adoption\"],\n      \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n        \"A clean-clone build/run recipe identifies required dependencies, representative commands, supported configuration, and ownership boundaries.\",\n        \"The final guide distinguishes physical adoption, scale-screen results, visual evidence, and restart equivalence.\",\n        \"Limits, unresolved drift/cost risks, deferred rich-world requirements, and negative outcomes are plainly stated.\",\n        \"Superseded candidate code and disposable probes are removed only after useful counterexamples and compact findings are preserved.\"\n      ],\n      \"plan_review\": null,\n      \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-laboratory\", \"AR-restart\", \"AR-population-screen\", \"AR-adoption\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"questions\": [],\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-experiments\",\n      \"title\": \"Bounded experiment and budget specification\",\n      \"description\": \"Proposed fixture geometry, units, physical scales, references, validity limits, error/cost budgets, horizons, and distinct prototype versus population-screen protocols.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-budgets\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-state-contract\",\n      \"title\": \"Authoritative state and ownership contract\",\n      \"description\": \"Shared data shapes, stable references, units, staged exchange interfaces, ownership rules, and rollback-relevant state.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-state-design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-mechanics-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Passive structural mechanics specification\",\n      \"description\": \"Chosen structural discretization, constitutive response, integration and failure limits, attachment interfaces, and worked mechanical references.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-mechanics-design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-contents-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Inertial chamber specification\",\n      \"description\": \"Geometry-derived pressure and energy, contents mass/inertia approximation, wall reactions, finite-port exchange meaning, and worked references.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-contents-design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-field-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Stationary flow and transport specification\",\n      \"description\": \"Discrete field equations, pressure constraints, species fluxes, outer conditions, convergence limits, geometry interface, and local reference calculations.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-field-design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-geometry-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Moving geometry and coupling specification\",\n      \"description\": \"Side-separated cut regions, swept-volume and pressure-work operators, support-change handling, bounded small-cell policy, and geometric reference calculations.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-geometry-design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-transfer-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Finite exchange and reaction specification\",\n      \"description\": \"Port/permeability laws, resource ownership transfers, donor limits, competing-request policy, reaction accounts, and worked examples.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-transfer-design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-actuation-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Local controller and paid-actuation specification\",\n      \"description\": \"Local sensing interface, deterministic cadence, actuator work and fuel law, negative-work policy, rollback behavior, and worked contraction cycle.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-actuation-design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-work-package\",\n      \"title\": \"Reconciled first physical work package\",\n      \"description\": \"Self-contained implementation contract incorporating the mechanism specifications, coupled schedule, global compatibility, staging/failure semantics, and proposed frozen experiments; its existence does not imply approval.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-schedule-design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-core\",\n      \"title\": \"Transactional simulation core\",\n      \"description\": \"Implemented authoritative state, stable handles, compact storage, accounts, staging, bounded interval advancement, and focused failure tests.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-core\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-passive\",\n      \"title\": \"Passive structural implementation\",\n      \"description\": \"Testable tissue/membrane mechanics and boundary/actuator attachment interfaces with focused reference fixtures.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-passive\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-chambers\",\n      \"title\": \"Pressure-bearing chamber implementation\",\n      \"description\": \"Geometry-coupled inertial contents with closed-chamber reference fixtures and explicit supported limits.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-chambers\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-field\",\n      \"title\": \"Stationary conservative field implementation\",\n      \"description\": \"Fluid, pressure, species transport, outer-boundary accounts, and stationary reference fixtures.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-field\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-geometry\",\n      \"title\": \"Shared geometric operator implementation\",\n      \"description\": \"Moving cut geometry, barrier connectivity, swept-volume operators, and independent geometric identity tests.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-geometry\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-moving-field\",\n      \"title\": \"Prescribed-boundary fluid package and findings\",\n      \"description\": \"Composed moving-boundary field implementation and bounded reference report, including local correctness, convergence, memory, and cost limitations.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-moving-field\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-passive-coupling\",\n      \"title\": \"Two-way passive coupled implementation\",\n      \"description\": \"Transactional structure–contents–fluid coupling, paired impulse/work exchanges, and passive coupled fixtures.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-passive-coupling\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-transfers\",\n      \"title\": \"Finite resource exchange implementation\",\n      \"description\": \"Ports, permeability, reactions, donor-limited paired transfers, and focused conservation and exhaustion tests.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-transfers\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-actuators\",\n      \"title\": \"Resource-limited controller and actuator implementation\",\n      \"description\": \"Local sensing, deterministic control, paid mechanical requests, and loaded-cycle/fuel-exhaustion fixtures.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-actuators\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-prototype\",\n      \"title\": \"Runnable active coupled organism\",\n      \"description\": \"Seeded construction, headless commands, project-owned telemetry, and representative motion, pumping, and resource-limitation examples.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-prototype\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-adoption\",\n      \"title\": \"Representative coupled qualification report\",\n      \"description\": \"Predeclared refinement, accumulated-error, behavior, and full-cost campaign findings, including rejection or uncertainty where warranted; not an approval record.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-adoption\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-contact-design\",\n      \"title\": \"Supported laboratory contact specification\",\n      \"description\": \"Bounded membrane/terrain contact, friction, narrow-gap compatibility, collision failure policy, worked references, and event-cost limits.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-contact-design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-contact\",\n      \"title\": \"Shared-world contact implementation\",\n      \"description\": \"Transactional contact consistent with fluid barriers and a small interacting-organism fixture.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-contact\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-population-screen\",\n      \"title\": \"Interacting laboratory scale-screen report\",\n      \"description\": \"Reproducible 16-organism fixture and measured active work, complete cost, memory, interaction behavior, and explicit limits on scale/endurance claims.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-population-screen\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-laboratory\",\n      \"title\": \"Inspectable prototype laboratory\",\n      \"description\": \"Thin visual application with pause/step inspection, meaningful overlays, and inspected snapshots correlated with semantic state.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-presentation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-restart\",\n      \"title\": \"Restart and recording workflow\",\n      \"description\": \"Explicit serialization adapters, continuation-equivalence checks, seeded replay recipe, and complete recording throughput accounting.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-restart\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-delivery\",\n      \"title\": \"Bounded foundation delivery guide\",\n      \"description\": \"Independent build/run instructions, demonstrations, supported approximation, qualification conclusions, retained counterexamples, and clearly deferred requirements.\",\n      \"produced_by\": \"T-handoff\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "target_revision": 0
    },
