                    "raw_response": "{\n  \"base_revision\": 1,\n  \"outcome\": \"propose_changes\",\n  \"reason\": \"The requested sequencing improvements are justified before implementation: qualify the two-way passive foundation before resource/activity work, and separate stationary flow from production species transport. These edits preserve human approval, the later active adoption campaign, and the population gate without asserting numerical results.\",\n  \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n  \"changes\": [\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Make the early passive decision explicit without replacing later adoption gates.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"decision\", \"id\": \"D-gates\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"decision\",\n            \"value\": \"Require a human-approved first work package, favorable prescribed-boundary review before two-way coupling, favorable bounded two-way passive qualification review before production species transport and resource/activity implementation, reviewed representative active coupled adoption evidence, and a separate population screen.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"rationale\",\n            \"value\": \"Design approval, experiment completion, passive feasibility, active numerical adoption, and scale claims are distinct decisions. Negative or inconclusive qualification findings do not release dependent work.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Specify the early campaign before human approval rather than inventing thresholds when it runs.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"task\", \"id\": \"T-budgets\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"context\",\n            \"value\": \"Use A-scope/A-hardware/A-screen and D-contract. Define the smallest two-chamber contractile organism that swims and pumps through finite ports, with nutrient exchange and fuel use; it need not represent a named substance. Specify consistent 2D units, shapes, coefficients, minimum features, fixed resolution family, initial conditions, species and energy meanings, and environmental outer conditions. Define the bounded two-way passive campaign, active prototype campaign, and later 16-organism screen separately; do not adopt the 256-organism workload. For passive qualification, predeclare closed-port references, repeated externally loaded/released and unforced relaxation cycles, refinement comparisons, local and cumulative error budgets, rollback checks, complete coupled cost, timescale-derived horizons, compute limits, extension rules, and rejection/inconclusive conditions. Any bounded tracer probe tests geometric remapping only, not production species transport. Numerical tolerances are proposals for human approval, not facts supplied by the vision.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Include the new passive protocol in the existing shared experimental contract.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"artifact\", \"id\": \"AR-experiments\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"description\",\n            \"value\": \"Proposed fixture geometry, units, physical scales, references, validity limits, error/cost budgets, horizons, and distinct bounded two-way passive, active prototype, and population-screen protocols, including refinement, stopping rules, and limits of any geometric tracer probes.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Retain the shared design while making the two implementation stages and their interface explicit.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cb5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"task\", \"id\": \"T-field-design\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"context\",\n            \"value\": \"Choose the discrete incompressible liquid momentum/pressure formulation, viscosity treatment, face fluxes, and conservative advection/diffusion for the declared species. Specify compatible open/pressure outer conditions, pressure null-space treatment where applicable, and initial/boundary data. Keep geometry operators abstract only at the explicit interface consumed by T-geometry-design. Delineate independently testable stationary-flow and species-transport contracts: flow exposes accepted fluid volumes, connectivity and face fluxes; transport owns species amounts and uses those same operators without duplicating fluid ownership. Specify transport staging, positivity, boundary accounts and moving-region remapping. Stationary and passive flow must run without production species transport; bounded geometric tracer probes are reference diagnostics, not a second production transport implementation.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Keep T-field as the continuing stationary-flow implementation; move species-specific work to its own task.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"task\", \"id\": \"T-field\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\"field\": \"title\", \"value\": \"Implement stationary conservative fluid flow\"},\n          {\n            \"field\": \"context\",\n            \"value\": \"Implement the approved stationary momentum, pressure and viscosity equations on AR-core with prescribed static geometry and pressure/open boundaries. Expose fluid volumes, connectivity and face fluxes for later moving geometry and species transport. Production species advection/diffusion, chamber transfers and reactions are excluded and must not be prerequisites for running stationary flow.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n            \"value\": [\n              \"Stationary pressure and channel flow meet the approved local-field and global-balance references.\",\n              \"Fluid mass, momentum and work include explicit boundary source/sink accounts.\",\n              \"Pressure convergence, iteration ceilings, memory, and complete field-step cost are recorded at prescribed resolutions.\",\n              \"Unconverged pressure and inadmissible fluid state reject the staged update.\",\n              \"The stationary-flow target runs independently of production species transport and exposes the approved geometry/flux interface.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Keep the continuing fluid artifact separate from the later species implementation.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"artifact\", \"id\": \"AR-field\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"description\",\n            \"value\": \"Stationary fluid momentum, pressure and viscosity implementation, outer-boundary mass/momentum/work accounts, geometry/face-flux interfaces, and stationary flow reference fixtures. Does not include production species transport.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Preserve moving-geometry transport checks without depending on the deferred species solver.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"task\", \"id\": \"T-moving-field\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"context\",\n            \"value\": \"Compose AR-field and AR-geometry with analytic boundary trajectories, independently of production species transport. Check local displaced volume and geometric remapping with analytic references and, where required by the approved protocol, a bounded passive tracer probe using the production geometry/flux operators. Keep that probe outside production transport; it cannot qualify nutrient advection/diffusion or reactions. Use simulation-health capability, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md and .agents/skills/bitloop-development/references/simulation-health-diagnostics.md for approved horizons and temporary probes; project oracles must be implemented. Retain negative or inconclusive outcomes as valid experiment results.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n            \"value\": [\n              \"Uniform-pressure equilibrium, free expansion, sealed moving barriers, moving corners, and support changes are tested across approved refinements.\",\n              \"Local displaced volume, geometric remapping and wall work are checked independently of global balances; any tracer probe records its bounded scope and does not imply production species acceptance.\",\n              \"Timestep, pressure convergence, small-cell work, memory, and complete prescribed-boundary cost are reported against approved limits.\",\n              \"The report identifies failed, passed, and inconclusive conditions and does not equate experiment completion with adoption.\",\n              \"The prescribed-boundary campaign runs without the production species solver.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Clarify the guarantees available to passive coupling consumers.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"artifact\", \"id\": \"AR-moving-field\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"description\",\n            \"value\": \"Composed moving-boundary fluid implementation and bounded reference report covering local displaced volume, geometric remapping, wall work, convergence, memory and cost limitations. Records any bounded tracer probe separately; does not establish production species-transport correctness or imply favorable review.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Distinguish focused coupling implementation checks from the subsequent feasibility campaign.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"task\", \"id\": \"T-passive-coupling\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"context\",\n            \"value\": \"Proceed only after favorable review of AR-moving-field. Implement the approved coupling schedule and paired impulse/work interfaces with closed chamber ports; no production species solver, transfers, reactions or active biology is required. Retain the focused passive fixtures and rollback/cost checks for T-passive-qualification; these implementation checks do not release downstream resource/activity work. Use simulation-health via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/simulation-health.md and references/simulation-health-diagnostics.md under .agents/skills/bitloop-development.\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Add the missing bounded two-way passive feasibility decision before substantial downstream reliance.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cb5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"add_task\",\n        \"task\": {\n          \"id\": \"T-passive-qualification\",\n          \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n          \"title\": \"Qualify the two-way passive foundation\",\n          \"goal\": \"Determine whether two-way structure–contents–fluid coupling warrants production species transport and resource/activity implementation.\",\n          \"context\": \"Consume AR-passive-coupling and the human-approved AR-work-package. Run its bounded passive protocol with closed ports and no production species solver, reactions, controllers or actuators. Use passive equilibrium, translation/rotation, free expansion, compression/recovery, sealed moving boundaries and supported support changes. Repeated externally loaded/released cycles must account for imposed work; unforced relaxation must remain distinct. Compare approved resolutions/timesteps at equal simulated duration. Use simulation-health and traces through their .mindgraph/project_capabilities hint files and the corresponding simulation-health-diagnostics.md and tracing-diagnostics.md references under .agents/skills/bitloop-development. Implement required physical oracles and project telemetry; capabilities do not supply them automatically. Retain configurations, commands, numerical observations, limits and compact evidence under .codex/runs and in supported MindGraph result fields. Do not weaken budgets or infer favorable review from report completion.\",\n          \"components\": [\"C-evidence\", \"C-state\", \"C-structure\", \"C-contents\", \"C-field\", \"C-interface\"],\n          \"depends_on\": [\"T-passive-coupling\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n          \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n            \"The report compares approved passive references, repeated cycles and refinements using predeclared local and cumulative budgets for pressure, geometry, displacement, momentum reactions and wall work.\",\n            \"Passive propulsion, cyclic gain, weak-motion loss, feature collapse and unresolved drift are assessed; physical dissipation and numerical residual remain distinct.\",\n            \"Hard monitors and selected committed-state inspections cover approved relaxation, forcing and accumulation horizons; stopping, extension and remaining uncertainty are recorded.\",\n            \"Injected coupling failures demonstrate rollback of mechanics, contents, geometry-dependent state, fluid and committed time, including bounded retry exhaustion.\",\n            \"Complete coupled cost and memory include staging, geometry, pressure/coupling solves, safety checks, retries and commit; hardware, build, precision, worker configuration and actual work counts are reported.\",\n            \"Passed, failed and inconclusive conditions and counterexamples are retained. Completing the bounded campaign does not establish adoption or release dependent work; negative or inconclusive findings require review before progression.\"\n          ],\n          \"plan_review\": {\n            \"question\": \"Does the bounded two-way passive evidence support D-method at the approved local/cumulative quality and complete cost, or must the foundation change before production species transport and resource/activity implementation?\"\n          },\n          \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-passive-coupling\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Keep qualification evidence distinct from implementation and approval.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"add_artifact\",\n        \"artifact\": {\n          \"id\": \"AR-passive-qualification\",\n          \"title\": \"Two-way passive qualification report\",\n          \"description\": \"Bounded passive references, repeated-cycle/refinement comparisons, local and cumulative errors, rollback observations, complete coupled cost and memory, retained counterexamples and limitations. Includes negative or inconclusive findings; its existence is not approval.\",\n          \"produced_by\": \"T-passive-qualification\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Establish production species transport independently against the reviewed moving/passive foundation.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cb5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"add_task\",\n        \"task\": {\n          \"id\": \"T-species\",\n          \"parent_id\": \"T-foundation\",\n          \"title\": \"Implement conservative species transport\",\n          \"goal\": \"Deliver independently testable field species advection, diffusion and moving-region transport before finite resource exchange.\",\n          \"context\": \"Proceed only after favorable T-passive-qualification review. Implement the species contract reconciled into the human-approved AR-work-package from AR-field-design and AR-geometry-design. Use AR-field and AR-geometry interfaces and AR-passive-coupling for moving two-way integration; AR-core owns staging and authoritative amounts. Transport the declared species using accepted fluid volumes, side connectivity and face fluxes without duplicating fluid mass or introducing a second geometry path. Exclude chamber ports, permeability, reactions, controllers and actuation, which remain downstream. Bounded earlier tracer probes are diagnostic references, not an alternative production solver. Keep focused stationary references and representative moving/passive integration tests with this implementation. Use simulation-health and traces via their .mindgraph/project_capabilities hint files and corresponding references under .agents/skills/bitloop-development for temporal checks; implement project oracles and telemetry and retain substantive observations.\",\n          \"components\": [\"C-field\", \"C-interface\", \"C-state\"],\n          \"depends_on\": [\"T-core\", \"T-field\", \"T-geometry\", \"T-passive-coupling\", \"T-passive-qualification\", \"T-schedule-design\"],\n          \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n            \"Stationary uniform advection and diffusion meet approved local-field, refinement and global-balance references independently of resource exchange or active biology.\",\n            \"Species positivity, donor availability and explicit outer-boundary source/sink accounts follow the approved transport contract.\",\n            \"Prescribed moving barriers and representative two-way passive trajectories preserve local transported amounts and side separation across supported support changes, moving corners and narrow passages.\",\n            \"Inadmissible transport rejects the staged update; forced rejection leaves species, coupled state and committed time unchanged.\",\n            \"Transport and complete coupled-step work and memory are measured at approved resolutions and horizons, including staging, safety checks and retries; earlier passive qualification is not presented as species acceptance.\"\n          ],\n          \"plan_review\": null,\n          \"input_artifacts\": [\"AR-core\", \"AR-field\", \"AR-geometry\", \"AR-passive-coupling\", \"AR-passive-qualification\", \"AR-work-package\"]\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Provide one shared production transport deliverable, distinct from design and qualification evidence.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"add_artifact\",\n        \"artifact\": {\n          \"id\": \"AR-species\",\n          \"title\": \"Conservative species transport implementation\",\n          \"description\": \"Field species amounts, conservative advection/diffusion, positivity and outer-boundary accounts, moving-region transport using shared geometry/flux operators, and focused stationary and passive-coupled tests. Excludes ports, permeability, reactions and actuation.\",\n          \"produced_by\": \"T-species\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Block resource exchange until passive review and transport implementation, preserving existing prerequisites.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"task\", \"id\": \"T-transfers\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"context\",\n            \"value\": \"Proceed only after favorable T-passive-qualification review and completion of T-species. Consume AR-passive-qualification for the supported foundation and its limits; report existence alone does not release work. Implement the transfer/reaction portion of AR-work-package against AR-species and the existing field, chamber and geometry interfaces. Exercise static or prescribed geometry first, then verify paired exchanges in the supported moving/passive configuration. Exclude rupture, growth, repair, and heat.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"depends_on\",\n            \"value\": [\"T-core\", \"T-chambers\", \"T-field\", \"T-geometry\", \"T-schedule-design\", \"T-passive-qualification\", \"T-species\"]\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"input_artifacts\",\n            \"value\": [\"AR-core\", \"AR-chambers\", \"AR-field\", \"AR-geometry\", \"AR-work-package\", \"AR-passive-qualification\", \"AR-species\"]\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"Make the active prototype consume the extracted transport implementation explicitly while retaining existing integration inputs.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\"human-306e711065517ba8cc9d8cbf5862d3da\"],\n      \"edit\": {\n        \"op\": \"update_fields\",\n        \"target\": {\"kind\": \"task\", \"id\": \"T-prototype\"},\n        \"fields\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"context\",\n            \"value\": \"Compose AR-passive-coupling, AR-species, AR-transfers, and AR-actuators using the approved fixture, after the favorable passive qualification required by their dependency chain. Use bitloop and traces capabilities via .mindgraph/project_capabilities/bitloop.md, .mindgraph/project_capabilities/traces.md, .agents/skills/bitloop-development/SKILL.md and its references/tracing-diagnostics.md. Keep Substrate/Substrate.h and .cpp thin; place construction and telemetry outside core ownership. Passive qualification does not replace this active integration or the later T-adoption campaign.\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"depends_on\",\n            \"value\": [\"T-passive-coupling\", \"T-transfers\", \"T-actuators\", \"T-schedule-design\", \"T-species\"]\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"input_artifacts\",\n            \"value\": [\"AR-passive-coupling\", \"AR-transfers\", \"AR-actuators\", \"AR-work-package\", \"AR-species\"]\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"task_actions\": [],\n  \"follow_up\": null\n}",
